# already fixed in the vendored copy: pdfjs-dist 2.10.0 reported from
# apps/files_pdfviewer/js/vendor/pdfjs/package.json (files_pdfviewer v1.1.2). The
# /FontMatrix fix was backported into build/pdf.js and build/pdf.worker.js in
# owncloud/files_pdfviewer#351 (v1.1.1) and is guarded there by a regression test
# against a PoC PDF. The vendored package.json deliberately keeps reporting the
# upstream version so scanners can inventory the library, which is why the row
# appears at all -- v1.1.1 shipped no package.json and so was never scanned.
# Drops out when the vendored copy is regenerated from pdf.js >= 4.2.67
# (owncloud/files_pdfviewer#363).
CVE-2024-4367

# not fixed in this bundle: google.golang.org/grpc v1.84.0-dev, reported from
# apps/migrate_to_ocis/bin/rclone_linux_amd64 (migrate_to_ocis v3.0.2, which
# bundles upstream rclone v1.75.1). rclone v1.75.2 carries the fixed
# v1.85.0-dev, but no released migrate_to_ocis bundles it yet. Not reachable:
# the panic is in the xDS routing interceptor, installed only by servers built
# with xds.NewGRPCServer(), and needs an inbound RPC carrying neither :authority
# nor Host -- the app shells out to `rclone sync` and `rclone obscure` and never
# serves gRPC. Do not carry this into the next 11.0.x file once its bundle ships
# a migrate_to_ocis with rclone >= v1.75.2 (owncloud/migrate_to_ocis#74).
CVE-2026-84445

# not fixed in this bundle: Go standard library go1.26.8 and golang.org/x/net
# v0.57.0, reported from the same apps/migrate_to_ocis/bin/rclone_linux_amd64
# (rclone v1.75.1). rclone v1.75.2 is built with the fixed go1.26.9 and x/net
# v0.60.0, but no released migrate_to_ocis bundles it yet.
# CVE-2026-78667 (Range header parsing in FileServer/ServeContent/ServeFile) and
# CVE-2026-97031 (ECH extension handling in a crypto/tls server) are server-side
# only and not reachable: the app runs rclone purely as a client.
# CVE-2026-78669 (HTTP/2 SETTINGS flood) does affect clients. It needs a
# malicious HTTP/2 peer: the oCIS target or the ownCloud source URL rclone is
# pointed at. If `occ migrate:to-ocis:init` ran with --insecure (-k), the app
# stores that and passes rclone --no-check-certificate for both remotes on
# every later files run, so anyone on the network path to either can be that
# peer. The impact is CPU load on the app server across the files migration,
# which runs one `rclone sync` per user and can take hours. No data is exposed.
# Do not carry these into the next 11.0.x file under the same condition as
# CVE-2026-84445 above.
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031

# not fixed in this bundle: Go standard library go1.26.8, reported from the same
# apps/migrate_to_ocis/bin/rclone_linux_amd64 (rclone v1.75.1). Fixed in
# go1.26.10, which no rclone release is built with yet (v1.75.2 uses go1.26.9).
# GO-2026-6809 adds a crypto/x509 denylist of compromised intermediate CAs. rclone
# is only a client here, so the exposure is a man-in-the-middle presenting a chain
# through such an intermediate while an admin runs the files migration
# (`occ migrate:to-ocis:migrate:files`, the only step where rclone connects). With
# --insecure (-k) certificates are not verified at all, so the denylist would not
# help there either. Do not carry this into the next 11.0.x file once its bundle
# ships a migrate_to_ocis whose rclone is built with go >= 1.26.10.
CVE-2026-111943
